  "name": "Night Feast scales Bloodbolt from Rage before its cast cost (#2051)",
  "contract": "Night Feast 563736 increases Bloodbolt damage by 1% per point of Rage and increases its Rage cost by 10. Bloodbolt 578305 is the rank a level-80 Bloodmage owns. Rage is stored in tenths, so 800 is 80 points and the damage multiplier is 1.8. Bloodbolt costs 30 Rage without Night Feast and 40 with it, so post-cast Rage is 50 and 40 respectively. Rage is snapshotted before the native cost is deducted; this scenario compares four direct hits at the same pre-cast Rage with and without Night Feast. Every fixture carries spell_crit_rating 100000, so all eight hits of a comparison crit and the critical multiplier cancels in the ratio of totals; summing only noncritical hits let one ordinary crit change how many hits a side summed, which read 1.35 (three against four) or 2.41 (four against three) instead of about 1.8.",
